    content: "# IBPS PO & Clerk 4-in-1 Document Guidelines: Photo, Signature, Thumb & Handwritten Declaration (2026)\n\nEvery year, over 3.5 million graduates apply for banking careers through the Institute of Banking Personnel Selection ([ibps.in](https://www.ibps.in)) across IBPS PO, Clerk, SO, and Regional Rural Bank (RRB) cycles. Unlike most competitive examinations that require only two assets, IBPS mandates a strict **4-in-1 document upload process**: passport photograph, scanned signature, left thumb impression, and a customized handwritten declaration. Uploading any asset with incorrect ink color, dimension mismatch, or capital letter handwriting results in immediate registration disqualification. You can prepare all 4 assets conforming to official IBPS standards using Kagazo's [IBPS Photo & Signature Resizer](https://kagazo.in/tools/ibps-photo-signature-resizer), [Thumb Impression Resizer](https://kagazo.in/tools/thumb-impression-resizer), and [Handwritten Declaration Scanner](https://kagazo.in/tools/handwritten-declaration-scanner).\n\n## Key Takeaways\n\n- **Asset 1 (Photograph):** 200 × 230 pixels, file size strictly between **20 KB and 50 KB**, light-coloured or white background, no cap or dark glasses.\n- **Asset 2 (Signature):** 140 × 60 pixels, file size strictly between **10 KB and 20 KB**, signed strictly with **black ink pen** on white paper.\n- **Asset 3 (Left Thumb Impression):** 240 × 240 pixels (3 × 3 cm), file size strictly between **10 KB and 20 KB**, made using **blue or black ink pad**.\n- **Asset 4 (Handwritten Declaration):** 800 × 400 pixels (10 × 5 cm), file size strictly between **50 KB and 100 KB**, written strictly in **English with black ink**.\n- **Zero Capital Letters Rule:** Neither the signature nor the handwritten declaration may be written in capital BLOCK letters. Capitalized declarations are treated as impersonation and rejected.\n\n---\n\n## What Is the Exact Official Text for IBPS Handwritten Declaration 2026?\n\n**The official IBPS handwritten declaration must be written in the candidate's own handwriting in English using black ink on clean white unruled A4 paper without block capitals.**\n\nThe verbatim text prescribed in official IBPS notifications on [ibps.in](https://www.ibps.in) is as follows:\n\n> *\"I, _______ (Name of the candidate), hereby declare that all the information submitted by me in the application form is correct, true and valid. I will present the supporting documents as and when required.\"*\n\n### Critical Compliance Rules:\n1. **Self-Handwriting Mandatory:** The declaration must be penned by the applicant themselves. If a scribe or cyber café operator writes the text, the application is summarily rejected during biometric document verification.\n2. **Strictly English Language:** Declarations submitted in Hindi, Tamil, Telugu, or any regional language are not accepted under central IBPS guidelines.\n3. **Ink Color:** The declaration must be written strictly using a **black ink ballpoint or gel pen**. Blue ink is explicitly rejected for the declaration text.\n4. **No Capital Letters:** Writing the entire sentence in uppercase (capital) letters leads to automatic application cancellation.\n\n---\n\n## IBPS 4-in-1 Document Specifications Matrix\n\n| Asset Name | Allowed Dimensions | File Weight Limit | Ink / Color Specification | Allowed Format |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Passport Photo** | 200 × 230 Pixels (3.5 × 4.5 cm) | 20 KB to 50 KB | Natural colour, plain white background | Strictly JPG / JPEG |\n| **Scanned Signature** | 140 × 60 Pixels (3.5 × 1.5 cm) | 10 KB to 20 KB | Black Ink Pen on white paper | Strictly JPG / JPEG |\n| **Left Thumb Impression** | 240 × 240 Pixels (3.0 × 3.0 cm) | 10 KB to 20 KB | Blue or Black Stamp Pad | Strictly JPG / JPEG |\n| **Handwritten Declaration**| 800 × 400 Pixels (10 × 5 cm) | 50 KB to 100 KB | Black Ink Pen on white paper | Strictly JPG / JPEG |\n\n---\n\n## Left Thumb Impression (LTI) Guidelines for Banking Aspirants\n\n**Candidates must use a standard blue or black stamp pad on plain white paper, taking care to press evenly without smudging ridge patterns.**\n\n- **Right Thumb Exception:** If a candidate does not have a left thumb (due to physical disability or injury), the right thumb impression may be utilized, provided the applicant explicitly states this in the online portal profile.\n- **Scanning Quality:** Scanners must be calibrated to **200 DPI**. Smartphone camera captures must be cropped tightly to the stamp boundary to remove surrounding tabletop shadows using Kagazo's [Clean Document Scanner](https://kagazo.in/tools/clean-document-scanner).\n- **Undersize Rejection:** If a cropped thumb impression falls below 10.0 KB, the IBPS server blocks the submission. Kagazo automatically adds JFIF structural padding to lock the file securely at ~15 KB.\n\n---\n\n## How to Prepare All 4 IBPS Documents in 60 Seconds on Kagazo\n\n1. **Step 1:** Open [IBPS Photo & Signature Resizer](https://kagazo.in/tools/ibps-photo-signature-resizer) and select the **IBPS Photo** preset (auto-locks at 200×230 px and 35 KB).\n2. **Step 2:** Select the **IBPS Signature** preset and upload your black ink signature (auto-locks at 140×60 px and 15 KB).\n3. **Step 3:** Switch to [Thumb Impression Resizer](https://kagazo.in/tools/thumb-impression-resizer) to crop and calibrate your LTI to 240×240 px and 16 KB.\n4. **Step 4:** Open [Handwritten Declaration Scanner](https://kagazo.in/tools/handwritten-declaration-scanner) to boost handwriting contrast and compress to ~75 KB (within the 50–100 KB ceiling).\n5. All conversions complete 100% locally in device RAM with zero watermarks and zero privacy exposure.",
