    tags: ["e-Sevai","CSC Center","Cyber Cafe","Community Certificate","TNeGA","Tamil Nadu"],
    content: "# Tamil Nadu e-Sevai & CSC Center Operations: Multi-Page Revenue Certificate PDF Compression (Under 200 KB)\n\nCommon Service Centers (CSCs), Village Poverty Reduction Committees (VPRCs), and private cyber cafés across Tamil Nadu process over 150,000 citizen certificate applications every single day through the Tamil Nadu e-Governance Agency ([tnesevai.tn.gov.in](https://tnesevai.tn.gov.in)) and Revenue Department e-District ([edistricts.tn.gov.in](https://edistricts.tn.gov.in)) gateways. However, operators face constant upload rejections because the e-Sevai server strictly mandates that **supporting document attachments must not exceed 200 KB per file**. When operators scan citizen smart ration cards, Aadhaar cards, school Transfer Certificates (TC), and parent community certificates using standard office flatbed scanners or smartphone cameras, raw files frequently exceed 3 MB to 5 MB. In this operational manual, you will learn the exact document packaging workflow to compress multi-page revenue certificates under 200 KB while preserving digital signature validity using Kagazo's free [TN e-Sevai Certificate Prep](https://kagazo.in/tools/tn-esevai-certificate-prep) tool.\n\n## Key Takeaways\n\n- **Strict 200 KB Ceiling:** Every supporting proof uploaded to the Tamil Nadu e-Sevai portal must be a standalone PDF weighing strictly between **100 KB and 200 KB**. Files above 200 KB trigger automated server timeout errors.\n- **Legible QR & Certificate Serial:** Zonal Deputy Tahsildar digital signature stamps and encrypted QR barcodes must remain clearly scannable on smartphone barcode readers.\n- **Multi-Document Merging:** Parent community proofs, applicant school TCs, and self-declaration affidavits must be collated chronologically into a single, unified PDF rather than multiple disconnected image slips.\n- **Monochrome Thresholding:** Converting full-color Xerox copies to 200 DPI clean monochrome PDFs slashes document size by 87% without compromising evidentiary text clarity.\n- **Client-Side Data Protection:** In compliance with the Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act 2023, Kagazo executes all compression directly in device RAM memory, guaranteeing citizen Aadhaar and caste records are never stored on external cloud databases.\n\n---\n\n## Tamil Nadu Revenue Certificates Upload Limit Matrix\n\n| Certificate Name | Portal Gateway | Maximum Allowable Size | Required Supporting Documents |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Community Certificate (BC/MBC/SC/ST)** | TNeGA e-Sevai / Revenue | Strictly 200 KB (PDF) | Applicant Photo, Smart Ration Card, School TC, Father Community Proof |\n| **Nativity Certificate (பிறப்பிடச் சான்றிதழ்)** | TNeGA e-Sevai / Revenue | Strictly 200 KB (PDF) | 5-Year Residence Proof, EB Bill, Voter ID, Aadhaar Card |\n| **Income Certificate (வருமானச் சான்றிதழ்)** | TNeGA e-Sevai / Revenue | Strictly 200 KB (PDF) | Salary Slip / Employer Certificate, Bank Passbook, Ration Card |\n| **First Graduate (முதல் பட்டதாரி)** | TNeGA e-Sevai / TNEA | Strictly 200 KB (PDF) | Father/Mother School TCs, Sibling Non-Graduate Affidavit, Ration Card |\n| **Legal Heir (வாரிசுச் சான்றிதழ்)** | TNeGA e-Sevai / Revenue | Strictly 200 KB (PDF) | Death Certificate, Deceased Ration Card, Legal Heirs Aadhaar Cards |\n| **Destitute Widow (ஆதரவற்ற விதவை)** | TNeGA e-Sevai / Social Welfare | Strictly 200 KB (PDF) | Husband Death Certificate, Revenue Inspector Assessment, Income Proof |\n\n---\n\n## Why Generic Online PDF Compressors Fail on e-Sevai Portals\n\n**Generic compressors downsample raster images indiscriminately, turning the Tehsildar's 16-digit certificate serial number and barcode into blurry grey artifacts that fail verification.**\n\nWhen a Revenue Inspector (RI) or Zonal Deputy Tahsildar reviews an application on their administrative dashboard, they rely on high-contrast text and scannable QR verification:\n1. **Barcode Pixelation:** Standard online tools reduce resolution to 72 DPI, rendering the e-District QR code unreadable.\n2. **Missing Long-Term Validation (LTV):** When re-saving digitally signed PDFs through standard software, the cryptographic signature dictionary is stripped, destroying the valid CCA India green checkmark.\n3. **Privacy Violations:** Uploading citizen identity documents (containing Aadhaar numbers and community details) to international web converters violates UIDAI security circulars and exposes cyber café operators to liability.\n\n---\n\n## The 4-Step e-Sevai Compression Workflow for Cyber Cafes\n\n1. **Scan Documents at 200 DPI:** Set your flatbed scanner (Epson L3210, Canon G2010, or HP Ink Tank) to Grayscale or Black & White at 200 DPI resolution.\n2. **Merge Supporting Documents:** Group all pages for a single service into one file using Kagazo's [Merge Marksheets PDF](https://kagazo.in/tools/merge-marksheets-pdf) tool.\n3. **Calibrate to e-Sevai Preset:** Open [TN e-Sevai Certificate Prep](https://kagazo.in/tools/tn-esevai-certificate-prep) and select the **e-Sevai Revenue (100–200 KB)** preset.\n4. **Instant Download:** Kagazo's in-memory WebAssembly engine isolates background Xerox noise and outputs an optimized PDF safely locked at ~175 KB.\n5. **Upload & Submit:** Upload the file to [tnesevai.tn.gov.in](https://tnesevai.tn.gov.in) with zero upload timeouts.",
