    tags: ["Salary Slip","Income Tax","New Tax Regime","EPF","Payslip","Payroll"],
    content: "# Salary Slip Calculation & Format FY 2025–26: New Tax Regime, Standard Deduction & PF Rules\n\nA salary slip (or payslip) is the legal financial document issued monthly by an employer to an employee detailing gross earnings, statutory deductions, net take-home pay, and tax withholding. Whether you are applying for a bank home loan, submitting visa documentation, filing your Income Tax Return (ITR), or switching jobs, a properly structured salary slip is universally demanded. Following recent statutory amendments under Union Budget declarations, significant changes have been codified for **FY 2025–26 (Assessment Year 2026–27)**, including the enhanced **₹75,000 Standard Deduction** under the default New Tax Regime and revised tax slabs. In this comprehensive guide, explore the exact mathematical breakdown of basic pay, HRA, EPF, Professional Tax, and TDS, and generate print-ready payslips in seconds using Kagazo's free [Salary Slip Generator](https://kagazo.in/tools/salary-slip-generator).\n\n## Key Takeaways\n\n- **Enhanced Standard Deduction:** Under Section 16(ia) of the Income Tax Act, salaried employees opting for the default New Tax Regime receive a flat **₹75,000 standard deduction** (up from ₹50,000), reducing taxable salary automatically.\n- **New Tax Regime Default:** The New Tax Regime under Section 115BAC is the statutory default. Income up to ₹3,00,000 has 0% tax, with full rebate under Section 87A providing zero tax liability up to ₹7,75,000 gross salary (including standard deduction).\n- **EPF Statutory Mandate:** Employees' Provident Fund (EPF) deduction is statutorily fixed at **12% of (Basic Pay + Dearness Allowance)** for enterprises with 20+ employees under the Employees' Provident Funds and Miscellaneous Provisions Act, 1952.\n- **HRA Exemption Restrictions:** House Rent Allowance (HRA) exemption under Section 10(13A) is only claimable under the Old Tax Regime; under the New Tax Regime, HRA is fully taxable.\n- **100% In-Browser Privacy:** Kagazo compiles your salary slips entirely within client-side browser RAM; sensitive CTC figures and PAN numbers are never stored on any remote cloud database.\n\n---\n\n## Salary Slip Components: Earnings vs Deductions Breakdown\n\nEvery compliant Indian payslip comprises two distinct sections: **Gross Earnings** (credits) and **Statutory & Voluntary Deductions** (debits).\n\n| Component Category | Element Name | Statutory / Calculation Formula | Taxable Status (New Regime) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Earnings** | Basic Salary | Typically 40% to 50% of Total Cost to Company (CTC) | 100% Taxable |\n| **Earnings** | House Rent Allowance (HRA) | Usually 40% (non-metro) or 50% (metro) of Basic Pay | 100% Taxable (No exemption) |\n| **Earnings** | Dearness Allowance (DA) | Cost-of-living adjustment (mandatory for PSU/Govt) | 100% Taxable |\n| **Earnings** | Special Allowance | Residual balancing component of monthly CTC | 100% Taxable |\n| **Earnings** | Conveyance / Transport | Fixed travel allowance | 100% Taxable |\n| **Deductions** | Employee Provident Fund (EPF) | 12% of (Basic + DA) (capped or actual) | Deducted from Gross |\n| **Deductions** | Professional Tax (PT) | State-mandated tax (e.g., ₹200/mo or slab-based) | Statutory Deduction |\n| **Deductions** | Tax Deducted at Source (TDS) | Monthly estimated tax liability under Section 192 | Remitted to IT Department |\n| **Deductions** | Employee State Insurance (ESI) | 0.75% of Gross Wages (applicable if gross <= ₹21,000) | Health insurance fund |\n\n---\n\n## Income Tax Slabs for FY 2025–26 (New Tax Regime vs Old Tax Regime)\n\nWhen computing TDS on monthly salary slips, employers calculate tax based on the regime chosen by the employee:\n\n### Default New Tax Regime (Section 115BAC)\n- **₹0 to ₹3,00,000:** Nil (0%)\n- **₹3,00,001 to ₹7,00,000:** 5%\n- **₹7,00,001 to ₹10,00,000:** 10%\n- **₹10,00,001 to ₹12,00,000:** 15%\n- **₹12,00,001 to ₹15,00,000:** 20%\n- **Above ₹15,00,000:** 30%\n\n> **Section 87A Tax Rebate:** Salaried individuals with net taxable income up to ₹7,00,000 pay **ZERO tax**. With the ₹75,000 standard deduction, any employee earning up to **₹7,75,000 per annum** incurs zero tax liability under the New Regime.\n\n---\n\n## Net Take-Home Salary Calculation Formula\n\nThe mathematical formula to determine net in-hand salary deposited into an employee's bank account is:\n\n$$\\text{Net Take-Home Salary} = \\text{Gross Earnings} - (\\text{EPF} + \\text{Professional Tax} + \\text{ESI} + \\text{TDS} + \\text{Other Deductions})$$\n\n### Example: Monthly Calculation for ₹60,000 Gross Salary\n- **Basic Salary (50%):** ₹30,000\n- **HRA (40% of Basic):** ₹12,000\n- **Special Allowance:** ₹18,000\n- **Gross Earnings:** ₹60,000\n- **EPF (12% of Basic):** ₹3,600\n- **Professional Tax:** ₹200\n- **Income Tax (TDS under New Regime with rebate):** ₹0\n- **Total Deductions:** ₹3,800\n- **Net In-Hand Salary Deposited:** **₹56,200**\n\n---\n\n## Why Standard Word or Excel Payslips Get Rejected by Banks\n\nWhen applying for a SBI, HDFC, or ICICI home loan, credit card, or Schengen visa, underwriting algorithms automatically screen payslips for compliance:\n1. **Missing Corporate & Statutory Identifiers:** Bank underwriters reject slips lacking Company PAN, TAN, GSTIN, and EPFO Establishment Code.\n2. **Unbalanced Gross vs Net Math:** Discrepancies between basic pay percentages and PF deductions trigger immediate fraud flags.\n3. **Absence of UAN & Bank Details:** A genuine payslip must state the employee's Universal Account Number (UAN) and bank account IFSC details.\n4. **Unformatted Layouts:** Handwritten or plain text receipts are treated as non-institutional documents.\n\n---\n\n## How to Generate Professional, Audit-Ready Salary Slips on Kagazo\n\n1. **Navigate to Generator:** Open [Salary Slip Generator](https://kagazo.in/tools/salary-slip-generator).\n2. **Enter Employer & Employee Details:** Fill in Company Name, Logo, Employee Designation, Date of Joining, PAN, and UAN.\n3. **Configure Earnings & Deductions:** Enter Basic, HRA, Special Allowance, PF, and Professional Tax (the tool auto-balances gross totals).\n4. **Select Tax Financial Year:** Toggle FY 2025–26 to apply official standard deductions.\n5. **Instant PDF Download:** Export a clean, watermarked or corporate-branded vector PDF ready for loan verification and employee distribution.",
